# API logging

Log **key nodes** in application services and infrastructure adapters with `@api/infrastructure/logger` (LogTape). Never `console.log`.

## Where to log

| Node | Level | Example |
|------|-------|---------|
| Use case started / succeeded (mutations) | `info` | avatar uploaded, password changed, admin ban |
| External I/O succeeded (S3, auth admin API) | `info` | object key + public URL; action name |
| Recoverable failure (best-effort cleanup) | `warn` | delete previous avatar failed |
| Operation failure before rethrow | `error` | S3 write failed, Better Auth call failed |
| Expected client errors (validation, 404) | do not log | throw `AppException` only |

HTTP 401/403 stay in `auth-macro`. Route handlers stay thin — **do not** log there.

## How

Structured messages with named placeholders. Do **not** log secrets (passwords, access keys, file bytes).

```typescript
logger.info('Uploaded avatar for user {userId} to {imageUrl}', {
  userId,
  imageUrl,
});
logger.error('S3 upload failed, {key}, {error}', { key, error });
```

Keep `{error}` as the caught value. User-facing exception messages stay Chinese; log messages stay English.
